--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e9620f8c34305754d8cc9a7e49e852d9, type: 3}
  m_Name: Tutorial_en
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_LocaleId:
    m_Code: en
  m_SharedData: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 726c634dc02dbea4e96bad08be5823fa, type: 2}
  m_Metadata:
    m_Items: []
  m_TableData:
  - m_Id: 10823225344
    m_Localized: Good morning, Curator.\n I'm Leo, and I'll be with you to help you
      awaken this sanctuary.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 240109047808
    m_Localized: On your left is the shop. Here you can choose seeds to plant. You
      can also buy water and fertiliser, but be careful not to run out of petals.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 256873680896
    m_Localized: Oh, and don't forget to check the weather forecast, Curator. At
      the top right, you'll see the weather for the next few days. The weather can
      help you... or surprise you, so check it often.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 270651969536
    m_Localized: Curator... before we continue, there is something important to note.
      Biodiversity is the lifeblood of the Sanctuary. It increases every time you
      successfully grow different species, and decreases if any plants die. The more
      biodiversity you have, the more petals you will earn each day... and if you
      reach the goal, you will restore the Sanctuary!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 310036484096
    m_Localized: Well done, Curator! You have planted your first species in the Sanctuary.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 327434457088
    m_Localized: Now it's time to take good care of it. Use the watering can to water
      it and the fertiliser to enrich the soil. You can also use the spade to remove
      plants, which will help you recoup some of your investment. The better you
      look after the plot, the stronger the plant will grow.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 360934363136
    m_Localized: This is the plot information sheet. Here you can see how much water
      and fertiliser the soil has and how much sun exposure it receives. If there
      is a plant, you will also see its condition and needs.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 379183779840
    m_Localized: Wow, Curator! I see you've already mastered the basics of plant
      care. If you ever forget something, you can consult the quick guide by clicking
      on the question mark button above.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 386020495360
    m_Localized: This is the summary of the day, Curator. Here you can see how many
      petals you have earned, the bonuses for your garden, and the losses for dead
      plants or using the spade. You will also see if you receive extra water or
      fertiliser. Take a look every night to understand how the Sanctuary is evolving.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 406518059008
    m_Localized: Well, Curator... today we have a sunny day. The sun does not water
      the ground; on the contrary, it gradually dries it out.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 429381210112
    m_Localized: "Take a close look at the forecast in the top right corner: the
      sun can appear with three different intensities. \u2022 Intensity 1: sometimes
      dries 1 point of water from the plots. \u2022 Intensity 2: can dry 1 or 2 points.
      \u2022 Intensity 3: can dry up to 3 points of water."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 445046935552
    m_Localized: The sun alone does not kill plants, but if you let the soil get
      too dry, your plants will suffer from a lack of resources. Keep an eye on the
      water in your plots and water them when they need it.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 459987046400
    m_Localized: 'Today the sky is overcast, Curator. This weather is very calm:
      it neither waters nor dries the soil, regardless of its intensity.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 494560694272
    m_Localized: 'Think of it as a breather for the garden: you can take advantage
      of this time to plan, rearrange your plants, and prepare for tougher days ahead.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 514034847744
    m_Localized: Oh dear, Curator... it's raining at the Sanctuary today. Rain always
      increases the water content of the soil in all the plots.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 532028411904
    m_Localized: "Pay close attention to the forecast, because rain also has three
      intensities:\\n\u2022 Intensity 1: light rain, adds +2 water.\\n\u2022 Intensity
      2: moderate rain, adds +4 water.\\n\u2022 Intensity 3: heavy rain, adds +6
      water and can endanger weak plants."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 548642050048
    m_Localized: Light to moderate rain is perfect for reviving dry patches. But
      heavy rain can kill plants that are already in poor health. If you see heavy
      rain coming in the forecast, try to get your plants as healthy as possible
      before it arrives.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 565972914176
    m_Localized: Oh dear, Curator... it's hailing today. It's one of the most dangerous
      weather conditions for your garden.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 580728475648
    m_Localized: "Like rain, hail can fall with three intensities and also adds some
      water to the ground:\\n\u2022 Intensity 1: light hail, +1 water.\\n\u2022 Intensity
      2: moderate hail, +2 water.\\n\u2022 Intensity 3: heavy hail, +3 water and
      a very hard blow."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 597744766976
    m_Localized: The important thing about hail is not the water, but the damage
      it causes:\nAt any intensity, it can kill plants that are in poor health,\nand
      the stronger it is, the more even those that are only moderately healthy will
      suffer.\nIf you see hail coming in the forecast,\ntry to get your plants as
      healthy as possible before that day arrives.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 616304562176
    m_Localized: Curator... you have just received a strike. These are warnings that
      the Sanctuary is in danger. If you reach 5 strikes (yellow or red), the Sanctuary
      will collapse and you will lose the game.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 632662347776
    m_Localized: "Normal strikes appear when you neglect the garden:\\n\u2022 Every
      2 plants that die add up to 1 strike.\\n\u2022 And also if you go several days
      without planting\\n even though you have enough petals to do so."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 647162056704
    m_Localized: The good news is that normal strikes can be removed. If you keep
      at least three plants alive and go five days in a row without any dying, the
      Sanctuary will forgive one of your strikes.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 661791789056
    m_Localized: This time it's more serious, Curator...\nYou've run out of plants
      and petals\nto replant.\n\nThe Sanctuary has given you some petals to help
      you,\nbut in return you've received a permanent red strike.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 676891283456
    m_Localized: Permanent strikes can never be cleared. They still count towards
      the 5-strike limit, so try not to run out of garden space again.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 693374898176
    m_Localized: Well done, Curator! You have taken such good care of your garden
      for several days that the Sanctuary has decided to forgive you one normal strike.
      If you continue to keep your plants healthy, you will be able to clear more
      warnings.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 709200007168
    m_Localized: Curator... I see that one of your plants has been attacked by a
      pest. You will recognise it by the icon that appears above it. It does not
      kill it instantly, but it is a bad sign for the Sanctuary.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 724324667392
    m_Localized: As long as it has pests, that plant will not be able to recover
      its health, even if you water and fertilise it correctly. And if it is a fruit-bearing
      plant, it will stop bearing fruit even if it has pollinators nearby.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 743429722112
    m_Localized: "There are two ways to get rid of pests:\\n\u2022 Plant wildlife
      refuges nearby: they protect adjacent plots\\n and, over time, wildlife can
      clear the pest.\\n\u2022 Use your spade on the infected plant: you eliminate
      the plant and also the pest from that plot, but you lose part of your investment.
      Combine shelters, producers and pollinators to make your garden resistant to
      future pests."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 761666555904
    m_Localized: See, Curator? The wildlife in the shelter has cleared the pest from
      that plant. Shelter plants protect nearby plots and, over time, can cure pests
      in their area.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 779160997888
    m_Localized: If you have many important production facilities, it is worth surrounding
      them with wildlife refuges. This will prevent new pests from appearing, and
      if any do appear, the wildlife will have somewhere to live so that it can clean
      them up.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 794914803712
    m_Localized: When you use the shovel on a plant with pests, you eliminate the
      plant and also the pests from that plot. It's a quick solution when the infestation
      is out of control, but you'll lose some of the petals you invested. Use it
      to cut down on stubborn pests while redesigning the garden with more wildlife
      shelters around.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 810333065216
    m_Localized: You have planted a production company, Curator. It is the plants
      that generate petals, but they need a good environment to do so.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 825214455808
    m_Localized: "To produce fruit, they need to meet three conditions:\\n\u2022
      Be in good or moderate health.\\n\u2022 Be free of pests.\\n\u2022 Have pollinators
      nearby (from a healthy attractor)."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 838325850112
    m_Localized: Think of them as the economic heart of the Sanctuary. Protect them
      with wildlife shelters and place them in adequate sunlight so that they can
      give their best.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 855128231936
    m_Localized: You have planted a shade plant. Its function is to modify the light
      in nearby plots when it grows sufficiently.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 869820878848
    m_Localized: Shade can transform a sunny area into partial shade or full shade.
      This helps plants that suffer from too much sun, but can harm those that need
      direct light.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 880763817984
    m_Localized: If you place several shade plants around a plot, the accumulation
      can create very shady areas. Use them to adjust the sun exposure to the exact
      type that each species needs.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 900678373376
    m_Localized: You have just planted a pollinator attractor. These plants attract
      the life necessary for your fruit trees to bear fruit.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 933423304704
    m_Localized: Nearby plots will receive pollinators. Without them, producers will
      not generate petals even if they are healthy. Place them strategically to feed
      several producers at once.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 954843615232
    m_Localized: 'Remember: pollinators + healthy producers = strong economy. Also
      take care of attractors, because if they become ill or die, producers will
      no longer receive pollinators.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 977618685952
    m_Localized: You have planted a wildlife refuge. These plants attract animals
      that protect the Sanctuary.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 995645804544
    m_Localized: Wildlife prevents pests from appearing in nearby plots and can even
      cure existing pests over time.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1012976668672
    m_Localized: They are essential to ensure that your producers and attractors
      are not rendered useless. Distribute shelters around important areas to keep
      pests at bay.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 36095959846912
    m_Localized: 'Good morning, Curator!


      Your face looks unfamiliar... Is
      this your first day here?

      I''m Leo, your colleague at this sanctuary.

      Would
      you like me to help you get started?'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 36192206540800
    m_Localized: Guide me, Leo
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 36219884752896
    m_Localized: I'll manage
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  references:
    version: 2
    RefIds: []
